  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4a2b061e491659d4e8424ca22aacc1c7, type: 3}
  m_Name: Read_ZoneProfile_Power_Mid
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Hecton8.World.WorldExpeditionLoopProfile
  profileId: loop.profile.power.mid
  profileLabel: Power Mid Read
  entryBeat: Generator, relay, or load silhouettes make the local system legible
    from a distance.
  routineBeat: The player can quickly read source, transfer, and demand without being
    forced into one route.
  reliefBeat: A small stable pocket near the system gives room to inspect and plan.
  pressureBeat: Pressure comes from broken links, exposure, and the cost of stabilizing
    the chain.
  payoffBeat: 'The reward is regained leverage: safer nearby water, stronger utility,
    or a working support line.'
  exitBeat: Leaving should still feel readable through system memory, not through
    a fixed track.
  playerFreedomRule: The player can observe, repair, ignore, or return later depending
    on their needs.
  softProgressionPull: Visible system logic naturally tempts the player to follow
    power relationships.
  optionalDetourRule: Off-angle looks should still reveal useful system clues or
    side value.
  returnLogic: Returning later should feel worthwhile because the player remembers
    how the line behaved.
  masteryLogic: Mastery means seeing the whole power picture fast and acting only
    where it matters.
  playerPromise: Readable infrastructure that rewards understanding more than obedience.
  routeMemoryRule: Memory should latch onto the strongest source, the most obvious
    relay, and the hungriest load.
  failureMode: If source, transfer, and demand blur together, the system loses meaning.
